---
import LegalPage from "../layouts/LegalPage.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from "../data/site";
import { legal } from "../data/content";
---

<LegalPage
  eyebrow="Terms"
  title="Plain terms for a calm app."
  description="The terms of the Jamaal subscription and using the app."
  updated={legal.updated}
>
  <h2 id="subscription">The subscription</h2>
  <p>
    Jamaal is free for 14 days with everything included. After that it's one simple plan: $24.99 a year or $2.99 a
    month, in US dollars. The App Store shows the price in your local currency. One subscription covers Jamaal on
    iPhone, iPad and Mac.
  </p>
  <p>
    Payment is charged to your Apple ID. A subscription renews automatically unless you cancel at least 24 hours before
    the end of the current period. You can manage or cancel it at any time in your Apple ID account settings. Refunds
    are handled by Apple.
  </p>

  <h2 id="without">If you don't subscribe</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing is taken away. You can still tick things off, log habits, mark Anchors and run the timer. Adding, editing
    and Night Planning need a subscription. You can always export your data.
  </p>

  <h2 id="using">Using Jamaal</h2>
  <p>
    Jamaal is licensed to you, not sold. Your use of the app is also governed by Apple's standard Licensed Application
    End User License Agreement. Please don't copy, reverse engineer or resell the app.
  </p>
  <p>
    Jamaal is a planning tool. Its Wellbeing reading is a plain summary of what you did in the app, not medical or
    professional advice.
  </p>

  <h2 id="data">Your data</h2>
  <p>
    Your lists, habits and Anchors are yours. They are kept on your device and, if you use sync, in your own iCloud. See
    the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> for details.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms, and will change the date at the top when we do. If a change matters to your subscription,
    we'll say so in the app or by email.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
